1 Overview
**********

Forth is an interactive programming system.  fig-Forth is a Forth that
can be generated in many different version for many different operation
systems.  This file documents what you as a user needs to know for
using this particular version of fig-Forth once it is installed on your
system.

   fig-Forth consists of three files:
   *  forth.com_HOSTED_LINUX_(lina) : the program

   * fig-Forth.ps fig-Forth.html : the documentation

   * fig-Forth.blk : source for auxiliary programs

   These files are generated together by the generic system fig86.gnr.
The documentation only applies to the fig-Forth with which it goes.

   If your Forth doesn't fit description below get a new version.
*Note Rationale & legalese::.

   These are the features:,

   It is running in protected mode.It is running under MSDOS.Blocks are
allocated in files. Use DOS for I/O, and uses no obsolete MSDOS
features.A number has a precision of 32 bits.It is indirect threaded.

* Menu:

* Gentle Introduction:: For newbies to Forth. You don't want to read this.
* Rationale & legalese:: For experts. You don't want to read this.
* Manual::	   User manual
* Glossary::  	   Description of Forth words
* Glossary Index:: Find a Forth words in the glossary
