File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: PAD,  Next: PFA,  Prev: NFA,  Up: DICTIONARY

5.4.19 PAD
----------

Name: PAD

   Stackeffect: -- addr

   Attributes: L0

   Description: Leave the address of the text output buffer, which is a
fixed offset above `HERE'  .


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: PFA,  Next: SMUDGE,  Prev: PAD,  Up: DICTIONARY

5.4.20 PFA
----------

Name: PFA

   Stackeffect: nfa -- pfa

   Attributes:

   Description: Convert the name field address of a compiled definition
to its parameter field address.

   See also: `'' `CFA' `LFA' `NFA'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: SMUDGE,  Next: TRAVERSE,  Prev: PFA,  Up: DICTIONARY

5.4.21 SMUDGE
-------------

Name: SMUDGE

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Used during word definition to toggle the "smudge bit"
in a definitions' name field. This prevents an uncompleted definition
from being found during dictionary searches, until compiling is
completed without error.

   See also: `IMMEDIATE'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: TRAVERSE,  Next: VLIST,  Prev: SMUDGE,  Up: DICTIONARY

5.4.22 TRAVERSE
---------------

Name: TRAVERSE

   Stackeffect: addr1 n -- addr2

   Attributes:

   Description: Move across the name field of a fig-FORTH variable
length name field.  ADDR1 is the address of either the length byte or
the last letter.  If N=1, the motion is toward hi memory; if N=-l, the
motion is toward low memory. The ADDR2 resulting is address of the
other end of the name.

   See also: `NFA' `PFA'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: VLIST,  Next: WIDTH,  Prev: TRAVERSE,  Up: DICTIONARY

5.4.23 VLIST
------------

Name: VLIST

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: List the names of the definitions in the context
vocabulary.


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: WIDTH,  Prev: VLIST,  Up: DICTIONARY

5.4.24 WIDTH
------------

Name: WIDTH

   Stackeffect: -- addr

   Attributes: U

   Description: In fig-FORTH, a user variable containing the maximum
number of letters saved in the compilation of a definitions' name.  (
Characters not saved need not match in a dictionary search).  It must
be 1 thru 31, with a default value of 31. The name character count and
its natural characters are saved, up to the value in `WIDTH'  . The
value may be changed at any time within the above limits.


