5.8.2 +ORIGIN
-------------

Name: +ORIGIN

   Stackeffect: n -- addr

   Attributes:

   Description: Leave the memory address relative by N bytes to the
area from which the user variables are initialised, so one can access
or modify the boot-up parameters.  A user variable addresses with an
offset from the initialisation for U0, which is at `0 CELL+ +ORIGIN '.
This can be swapped to get a fresh set of user variables.  One can
access or modify the boot-up parameters, prior to saving a customised
boot image, or to change the initialisation by `COLD' .

   See also: `(ABORT)' `USER'


