   Stackeffect: n1 -- n1 (if zero) / n1 -- n1 n1 (non-zero)

   Attributes: L0

   Description: Reproduce N1 only if it is non-zero.  This is usually
used to copy a value just before `IF'  , to eliminate the need for an
`ELSE'  part to drop it.

   See also: `DUP'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: 2DUP,  Next: DROP,  Prev: -DUP,  Up: JUGGLING

