5.15 OPERATOR
=============

The wordset OPERATOR contains the familiar operators for addition,
multiplication etc.  The result of the operation is always an integer
number, so division can't be precise. The combination of `/'  and `MOD'  (remainder)
is such that you can get the original back: `n m /   m *  n m MOD   +'
allways has the value M . This is true for all Forth's.  On fig-Forth
the `/'  is a "symmetric division" , i.e.  `-n m /' give the same
result as `n m /', but negated.  The forgeoing rule now has the
consequence that `MOD n m' has 2M-1 possible outcomes instead of M .
This is very worrysome for mathematicians, who stick to the rule that
`MOD n m' gives a result in the range 0 ... M-1 ("floored division" ).

