5.19.1 !CSP
-----------

Name: !CSP

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Save the stack position in `CSP' . Used as part of the
compiler security.


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: ?COMP,  Next: ?CSP,  Prev: !CSP,  Up: SECURITY

5.19.2 ?COMP
------------

Name: ?COMP

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Issue error message if not compiling.

   See also: `?ERROR'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: ?CSP,  Next: ?EXEC,  Prev: ?COMP,  Up: SECURITY

5.19.3 ?CSP
-----------

Name: ?CSP

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Issue error message if stack position differs from
value saved in CSP .


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: ?EXEC,  Next: ?LOADING,  Prev: ?CSP,  Up: SECURITY

5.19.4 ?EXEC
------------

Name: ?EXEC

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Issue an error message if not executing.

   See also: `?ERROR'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: ?LOADING,  Next: ?PAIRS,  Prev: ?EXEC,  Up: SECURITY

5.19.5 ?LOADING
---------------

Name: ?LOADING

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Issue an error message if not loading

   See also: `?ERROR'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: ?PAIRS,  Next: ?STACK,  Prev: ?LOADING,  Up: SECURITY

5.19.6 ?PAIRS
-------------

Name: ?PAIRS

   Stackeffect: n1 n2 -

   Attributes:

   Description: Issue an error message if N1 does not equal N2 . The
message indicates that compiled conditionals do not match.

   See also: `?ERROR'


File: fig86.msdos32.info,  Node: ?STACK,  Next: CSP,  Prev: ?PAIRS,  Up: SECURITY

5.19.7 ?STACK
-------------

Name: ?STACK

   No stackeffect

   Attributes:

   Description: Issue an error message is the stack is out of bounds.

